  "content": {
    "id": "p44-q47-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "47",
    "prompt": "One of the roots of $6x^3+x^2+kx-12=0$ is a reciprocal of another.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p44-q47-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find the roots.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-\\dfrac32$, $-\\dfrac23$, $2$.",
          "worked": "Let the roots be $\\alpha$, $\\frac{1}{\\alpha}$ and $\\beta$. From the product of roots,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\alpha\\left(\\frac1\\alpha\\right)\\beta&=-\\frac{-12}{6}\\\\\\beta&=2.\\end{align*}$$\nUsing the sum of roots,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\alpha+\\frac1\\alpha+2&=-\\frac16\\\\\\alpha+\\frac1\\alpha&=-\\frac{13}{6}\\\\6\\alpha^2+13\\alpha+6&=0\\\\(3\\alpha+2)(2\\alpha+3)&=0\\\\\\alpha&=-\\frac23\\text{ or }-\\frac32.\\end{align*}$$\nThe roots are $-\\dfrac32$, $-\\dfrac23$ and $2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 96
      },
      {
        "id": "p44-q47-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Hence, find $k$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$k=-20$.",
          "worked": "Using the sum of roots in pairs,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{k}{6}&=\\left(-\\frac32\\right)\\left(-\\frac23\\right)+2\\left(-\\frac32\\right)+2\\left(-\\frac23\\right)\\\\\\frac{k}{6}&=1-3-\\frac43\\\\\\frac{k}{6}&=-\\frac{10}{3}\\\\k&=-20.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 56
      }
    ]
  },
